.Dd November 21, 2026
.Dt NVRM 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nvrm_enumerate ,
.Nm nvrm_close ,
.Nm nvrm_device_count ,
.Nm nvrm_device_get ,
.Nm nvrm_device_info_get ,
.Nm nvrm_device_refresh ,
.Nm nvrm_json_document ,
.Nm nvrm_json_schema ,
.Nm nvrm_info_nfields ,
.Nm nvrm_info_field
.Nd NVIDIA Resource Manager device discovery
.Sh LIBRARY
libnvrm
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In nvrm/nvrm.h
.Ft int
.Fn nvrm_enumerate "nvrm_ctx **ctxp" "const nvrm_enum_opts *opts" "char *err" "size_t errlen"
.Ft void
.Fn nvrm_close "nvrm_ctx *ctx"
.Ft unsigned
.Fn nvrm_device_count "const nvrm_ctx *ctx"
.Ft nvrm_device *
.Fn nvrm_device_get "const nvrm_ctx *ctx" "unsigned index"
.Ft const nvrm_device_info *
.Fn nvrm_device_info_get "const nvrm_device *dev"
.Ft int
.Fn nvrm_device_refresh "nvrm_device *dev"
.Ft int
.Fn nvrm_json_document "const nvrm_ctx *ctx" "FILE *fp"
.Ft int
.Fn nvrm_json_schema "FILE *fp"
.Ft unsigned
.Fn nvrm_info_nfields void
.Ft const nvrm_field *
.Fn nvrm_info_field "unsigned index"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm libnvrm
library lists the NVIDIA GPUs in the machine and describes each one, through
the Resource Manager (RM) of the NVIDIA kernel module.
It uses only the RM escape ioctls on
.Pa /dev/nvidiactl ;
it needs no Linux compatibility layer.
See
.Xr nvrm 7
for the model.
.Pp
.Fn nvrm_enumerate
selects a backend, opens the control device, checks that the kernel module is
the RM version the library was built for, lists the probed GPUs, attaches them,
queries each one and limits the descriptors for
.Xr capsicum 4 .
.Fa opts
may be
.Dv NULL ;
.Va opts->backend
names a backend
.Pq Dq rm No or Dq fake .
The backend is chosen in this order:
.Bl -enum -offset indent -compact
.It
.Va opts->backend ,
if given;
.It
else the environment variable
.Ev NVRM_BACKEND ,
which is ignored in a set-user-ID or set-group-ID process;
.It
else the backend with the highest score that is usable on the machine.
The fake backend is never chosen this way.
.El
On failure
.Fa *ctxp
is
.Dv NULL
and
.Fa err ,
if not
.Dv NULL ,
holds one line saying why.
.Pp
.Fn nvrm_close
releases everything, including the RM objects.
.Pp
.Fn nvrm_device_get
returns the device at
.Fa index ,
or
.Dv NULL .
.Fn nvrm_device_info_get
returns its description, a
.Vt nvrm_device_info .
Every member is an
.Vt nvrm_u64 ,
.Vt nvrm_str
or
.Vt nvrm_list :
a value, a reason code and a source.
A value is valid only when
.Fn NVRM_HAVE
is true; otherwise
.Va reason
says why it is not
.Pq see Fn nvrm_reason_id
and no number is made up.
.Pp
.Fn nvrm_device_refresh
queries the GPU again through the descriptors that are already open.
It works in capability mode.
It returns
.Dv NVRM_E_IO
when a system call to the driver failed (the affected values then carry the
reason
.Li os_call_failed ) ,
and 0 otherwise; a value the RM itself refuses is not an error of the call.
.Pp
.Fn nvrm_info_nfields
and
.Fn nvrm_info_field
describe the members of
.Vt nvrm_device_info
(group, name, kind, whether it reads in hex); the JSON output, the schema and
the text view of
.Xr nvrm-info 8
all walk this one table.
.Pp
.Fn nvrm_json_document
writes the whole description as one JSON line, schema
.Li nvrm-info/1 .
The related
.Fn nvrm_json_header ,
.Fn nvrm_json_device ,
.Fn nvrm_json_end
and
.Fn nvrm_json_error
write the records of the line stream.
.Fn nvrm_json_schema
writes the JSON Schema of all of them; it is generated from the same table as
the output.
Each returns 0, or \-1 if writing failed.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn nvrm_enumerate
returns 0 or one of
.Dv NVRM_E_NOBACKEND ,
.Dv NVRM_E_OPEN ,
.Dv NVRM_E_VERSION ,
.Dv NVRM_E_IO ,
.Dv NVRM_E_NOMEM ,
.Dv NVRM_E_INVAL ,
.Dv NVRM_E_NODEV ,
.Dv NVRM_E_CAPSICUM .
.Fn nvrm_strerror
and
.Fn nvrm_error_id
turn the code into text and a stable machine identifier.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width ".Ev NVRM_FAKE_PROFILE"
.It Ev NVRM_BACKEND
.Dq rm
or
.Dq fake .
.It Ev NVRM_FAKE_PROFILE
Comma list of fake GPUs:
.Dq discrete ,
.Dq unified ,
.Dq unknown ,
.Dq sparse .
.It Ev NVRM_FAKE_FAIL
Make a step of the fake backend fail:
.Dq open ,
.Dq version ,
.Dq list ,
.Dq nogpu ,
.Dq gpu_open ,
.Dq limit .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ".Pa /dev/nvidiactl"
.It Pa /dev/nvidiactl
RM control device.
.It Pa share/nvrm/schema/nvrm-info-1.schema.json
JSON Schema of the JSON output.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr capsicum 4 ,
.Xr nvrm 7 ,
.Xr nvrm-info 8
.Sh HISTORY
The library first appeared with the native NVIDIA graphics and compute stack.
